    "previous_model_response": "Since \\(OA=OB\\) are radii, \\(\\triangle AOB\\) is isosceles. Given \\(\\angle OAB=40^\\circ\\), we also have \\(\\angle ABO=40^\\circ\\).\n\nThus,\n\\[\n\\angle AOB=180^\\circ-40^\\circ-40^\\circ=100^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe inscribed angle \\(\\angle APB\\) subtending arc \\(AB\\) is half the corresponding central angle:\n\\[\n\\angle APB=\\frac12\\angle AOB=50^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nD"
  },
